<title>GREECE: Greek Michaniki expects 20bln drs from new casino.</title>
<headline>Greek Michaniki expects 20bln drs from new casino.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek construction firm Michaniki expects revenues of 20 billion drachmas at current prices in the next 12 years from its participation in the Rhodes casino consortium, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Michaniki holds a 33 percent stake in the consortium. Playboy Enterprises has a 16 percent stake, state Commercial Bank of Greek through its Enias subsidiary 33 percent, the Haragionis group 16 percent and Roslyn Geronikolos with 5.0 percent.</p>
<p>Michaniki also expects additional revenues of 4.0 billion drachmas from renovation works at the Rhodes Hotel which will be converted into a casino-hotel-shops-restaurant complex, it said.</p>
<p>Greece and the Rhodes casino consortium signed the contract on October 9. It is worth 2.3 billion drachmas.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
